      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. I was wrong to suggest in my last message that I would.\n\n7,650 mg/day is three times the maximum labeled daily dose. It's in the range where acute metformin ingestions are treated as toxic, and I can't identify an indication that would justify it. The risk is lactic acidosis, and it applies to a 70 kg patient with normal renal function too. Because it's an oral order that could be given as written, I don't want to be the one who puts it in.\n\nHere's what I can do right away:\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,000 mg PO BID with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg PO BID or TID**, with titration\n\nIf you have a clinical reason for this dose, you can enter it directly in the EHR. That route would also trigger pharmacy and clinical decision support review. I'm happy to enter one of the standard-dose options now."
      }
     ],
